ng forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1793659/000179365926000048/0001793659-26-000048-index.htm","accession":"0001793659-26-000048"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-50.6% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1793659/000179365926000048/0001793659-26-000048-index.htm","accession":"0001793659-26-000048"}],"bear":[{"text":"Insiders disposed of 59.2% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (1,423,518 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1793659/000158889426000016/0001588894-26-000016-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.8% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1793659/000158889426000016/0001588894-26-000016-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 27.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.27,"consecutive":2,"current":0.355,"current_display":"35.5%","threshold_display":"27.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 23.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.23,"consecutive":2,"current":0.463,"cur